Hello,

The end of the application period is coming up in two weeks (March 30).
Greg doesn't take any more patches from the mailing list after the end of
the application period, so the patches that count for your application are
essentially those that are accepted up to that time.

For the application, we are not looking for a major literary masterpiece.
Ideally an application should be concise and to the point, but should
accurately reflect the things that you have done.  It is not necessary to
list all the patches that can be found in the staging tree, but you may
want to summarize the range of more interesting patches that you have
submitted.

Also, there will be only one intern per project, so don't spend all of
your time on the small tasks of one single project, but instead do some
work on all of the projects that could be of interest to you.  And discuss
with the mentor a possible work timeline, not so much to nail things down,
but just so that everyone has a clear idea of what will be accomplished in
the project.

Please let me know if you have any questions.  I would also be happy to
review applications when they are ready.

julia

